(vector (map (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607172300-kotobase-query-protocol-extension.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607172210-kotobase-protocol-layer-extension.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607060100-kotoba-lang-reverse-domain-rename-batch2.edn")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607172500-kotobase-query-protocol-graphql-gremlin"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-17"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607172500: kotobase query-protocol extension, round 2 — GraphQL + Gremlin surfaces\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-17\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n**Scope**: `kotoba-lang` org — 2 new query-protocol repos\n**Depends on**: ADR-2607172300 (kotobase-query bridge — both new surfaces consume it), ADR-2607172210\n(protocol-layer-extension decision — the repo-layout/naming discipline this ADR follows)\n\n## Context\n\nFollowing the four-surface query-protocol batch (datomic-client-shim / org-postgresql-wire /\norg-opencypher-cypher / org-w3-sparql-protocol, ADR-2607172300 — all shipped, CI green, manifest\nregistered), the owner asked for two more: `graphql.kotobase.net`, `gremlin.kotobase.net`.\n\n**Naming precedent repeats from the SPARQL case**: `kotoba-lang/graphql` already exists as a\nsubstantial, real library (`graphql-clj` — SDL parsing, query parsing, structural validation, a pure\nfield-resolution executor over host-injected resolvers, zero third-party runtime deps, `.cljc`) — this\nis a reusable *engine*, not a protocol surface, same relationship `kotoba-lang/sparql` has to\n`org-w3-sparql-protocol`. The new protocol-surface repo therefore cannot use the bare `graphql` name\n(taken) and follows the same reverse-domain pattern used for `org-w3-sparql-protocol`: GraphQL's actual\ntransport spec is \"GraphQL over HTTP\" (graphql.github.io/graphql-over-http/, maintained by the GraphQL\nFoundation) — `org-graphql-http` names the spec being implemented (the HTTP binding), not just the\nquery language the existing `kotoba-lang/graphql` library already owns.\n\n`kotoba-lang` has no existing Gremlin/TinkerPop-adjacent repo. Apache TinkerPop is the real, citable\nopen-source project (Apache Software Foundation) that defines Gremlin — `org-apache-tinkerpop-gremlin`\nnames the owning project precisely, matching the full-name-when-recognizable convention already used\nfor `org-vrmc-vrm`/`org-bluesky-atproto` (specific consortium/company name, not a generic abbreviation).\n\nBoth surfaces are query interfaces over data other surfaces already give KRP Name/Content/Location\nidentities to — no new KRP identity mapping needed, same reasoning ADR-2607172300 used for its four\nsurfaces.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Repo layout\n\n| Item | Name | Depends on | Naming rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GraphQL over HTTP | `kotoba-lang/org-graphql-http` | `kotoba-lang/graphql` (existing SDL/executor library), `kotobase-query` | GraphQL over HTTP is the real spec being implemented; bare `graphql` name already taken by the library |\n| Gremlin | `kotoba-lang/org-apache-tinkerpop-gremlin` | `kotobase-query` | Apache TinkerPop is the real open-source project defining Gremlin |\n\n### `org-graphql-http` — v0.1 scope\n\nQuery-only (no mutations, no subscriptions — matches the read-only-first discipline every sibling\nquery surface in this project used: SPARQL protocol, Datomic shim, PostgreSQL's SELECT-only subset,\nCypher's MATCH-only subset). `POST /graphql` with the standard `{\"query\": \"...\", \"variables\": {...},\n\"operationName\": \"...\"}` request shape, `{\"data\": {...}, \"errors\": [...]}` response shape (GraphQL over\nHTTP spec). Field resolvers are backed by `kotobase-query`: a GraphQL type's fields resolve by querying\na materialized `kotobase-query` collection, with `visible?` (ADR-2607172300's required, non-defaulted\nredaction predicate) threaded through every resolver the same way the other three surfaces thread it.\nSchema definition (SDL) for v0.1 is provided by the deploy shell / test fixtures (this repo does not\ninvent a schema-from-IStore-collections auto-derivation — that's a real, separate feature a future ADR\ncould add, not required to ship v0.1).\n\n### `org-apache-tinkerpop-gremlin` — v0.1 scope\n\nGremlin traversal subset (deliberate boundary, same discipline as PostgreSQL's SQL subset and Cypher's\nMATCH subset): `g.V()` (scan a materialized collection), `.hasLabel(...)`/`.has(k, v)` (equality\nfilter), `.out(...)`/`.in(...)` (edge traversal — maps onto `kotobase-query`'s cross-collection join\ncapability, the same mechanism Cypher's relationship-pattern bonus scope uses), `.values(...)`\n(projection). No full Gremlin script evaluation (Groovy-shaped `eval` requests), no GraphBinary\n(GraphSON — JSON — only for v0.1, real TinkerPop Gremlin Server supports both; GraphSON is\ndramatically simpler and sufficient for a first pass), no transaction semantics, no\nlambda/closure-shaped traversal steps.\n\nTransport: real Gremlin Server protocol is WebSocket-based (`RequestMessage`/`ResponseMessage`\nenvelopes over GraphSON or GraphBinary). Same transport discipline as `kotoba-lang/nostr`'s\n`nostr.relay` (hand-rolled RFC 6455 handshake + frame codec over `node:net`+`node:crypto`, zero npm\ndeps, `.cljs`-only transport namespace separate from the pure `.cljc` traversal-translation core) — that\nrepo already proved this pattern works end-to-end (real cross-connection fan-out test, 2/2 scenarios).\nReuse that proof, don't re-derive the WebSocket handshake from scratch if `nostr.relay`'s transport code\ncan be adapted/vendored.\n\n## Rejected\n\n- **`graphql` bare name for the new repo** — already taken by the existing SDL/executor library;\n  reusing it (not renaming the library) is correct per the same \"each is a genuinely different thing\"\n  logic that kept `kotoba-lang/sparql` and `org-w3-sparql-protocol` as two separate repos.\n- **Schema-from-IStore-collections auto-derivation for GraphQL v0.1** — would be a nice capability but\n  is separable, real scope creep beyond \"ship a working GraphQL-over-HTTP surface\"; deploy-shell/test\n  fixture schemas are sufficient to prove the surface works.\n- **GraphBinary and full Gremlin script `eval` for v0.1** — GraphBinary is a real binary serialization\n  format with its own complexity budget; script `eval` would mean embedding a Groovy-shaped expression\n  evaluator, comparable to the SQL-parser lift `org-postgresql-wire` already took on for a different\n  language — one big new parser/evaluator per ADR is enough; GraphSON + a bytecode-shaped step subset\n  is the pragmatic v0.1 boundary.\n\n## Verification\n\nSame bar as every prior repo in this project: `nbb bin/run_tests.cljs` green (with a `.cljs`-only\ntransport-test split for `org-apache-tinkerpop-gremlin`, same as `org-ietf-sftp`/`org-postgresql-wire`/\n`kotoba-lang/nostr`), `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check` clean, CI green on both new repos.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607172300 (kotobase query-protocol extension — the four-surface precedent this ADR extends)\n- ADR-2607172210 (protocol-layer-extension decision — repo-layout/naming discipline)\n- ADR-2607060100 (reverse-domain rename batch 2 — the `org-<body>-<spec>` naming discipline)\n- `kotoba-lang/sparql` / `org-w3-sparql-protocol` (the library-vs-protocol-surface precedent this ADR's\n  GraphQL naming follows)\n- `kotoba-lang/nostr`'s `nostr.relay` (the WebSocket transport precedent `org-apache-tinkerpop-gremlin`\n  reuses)\n"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607172500: kotobase query-protocol extension, round 2 -- GraphQL + Gremlin surfaces"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))